1. fn-dsa (Rust implementation of FN-DSA / Falcon)
   Author:   Thomas Pornin
   Source:   https://github.com/pornin/rust-fn-dsa, commit 0629bb1 (2026-07-30);
             crates.io fn-dsa 0.4.0
   Licence:  The Unlicense (public-domain dedication), reproduced below.
   Ported (portable, non-SIMD code paths only; FLR replaced by native f64):
     - fn-dsa-sign/src/poly.rs: FFT, iFFT, FFT-domain polynomial operations, LDL, split and
       merge, the GM twiddle table                                   -> src/fft/
     - fn-dsa-sign/src/sampler.rs: SamplerZ (next, gaussian0, ber_exp) and ffSampling
       (ffsamp_fft_inner, split into a per-key tree builder and the sampling recursion; its
       per-attempt form is also copied into a unit test of src/ffsamp.rs). Modified: ber_exp
       uses the threshold 0 instead of a shift saturated at 63 when x >= 64 ln 2, and the
       width-3.1 base draw is new (a 192-bit table, drawn lazily)
                                                                     -> src/sampler.rs,
                                                                        src/ffsamp.rs
     - fn-dsa-sign/src/flr_native.rs: expm_p63 and its coefficients  -> src/sampler.rs
     - fn-dsa-sign/src/lib.rs: the basis, Gram matrix, target and rounding steps of
       sign_inner                                                    -> src/ffsamp.rs,
                                                                        src/sign.rs
     - fn-dsa-comm/src/shake.rs: Keccak-f[1600], SHAKE256, SHAKE256_PRNG -> src/prng.rs
     - fn-dsa-kgen/src/mp31.rs and poly.rs: arithmetic modulo 31-bit primes and the NTT
       (the CRT lift, the prepared products, the norm-tower inversion and the NTT check of
       fG - gF = q around them are new)                              -> src/ring/
     - the GAUSS0 table (fn-dsa-sign/src/sampler.rs:78-97)           -> src/tables.rs
     - fn-dsa-comm/src/codec.rs:7-71: trim_i8_encode and trim_i8_decode, generalised from i8
       to i16 coefficients, widths up to 16 bits and a zero-padded last byte
                                                                     -> src/codec.rs
     - fn-dsa-kgen/src/gauss.rs:30-81 (sample_f): the construction of the f, g sampler (a sign
       bit and a half-Gaussian CDT), adapted to a 128-bit table, a binary search, a lazy draw
       and no parity conditioning                                    -> src/keygen/gauss.rs
     - fn-dsa-kgen/src/lib.rs:266-315 (keygen_from_seed): the structure of the candidate loop
                                                                     -> src/keygen/trapgen.rs
     - fn-dsa-kgen/src/lib.rs:292-302 and src/ntru.rs:18-43: the two Gram-Schmidt norm tests,
       as formulas                                                   -> src/keygen/gs.rs
   Test vectors: tests/fixtures/sign/fndsa_sign512_kat.txt and fndsa_sampler512_kat.txt hold
   fn-dsa's own known-answer vectors (fn-dsa-sign/src/lib.rs:784-1151 and
   fn-dsa-sign/src/sampler.rs:646-2816), extracted by tools/sign/extract_fndsa_kats.py;
   tests/fixtures/parity/fndsa_vrfy_kat.txt holds its verification known-answer vectors
   (fn-dsa-vrfy/src/lib.rs:419-914), extracted by tools/parity/extract_fndsa_vrfy_kats.py.
   The fn-dsa and fn-dsa-comm crates are also dev-dependencies (test and benchmark only).

